les on any sampling trip.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t3-ehp0115-001040" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p> <italic>Enterococcus</italic> spp. isolated from ground-water, surface water, or manure pits located around or beneath a swine CAFO.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Enterococcus</italic> spp. source</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No. of isolates (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Up-gradient groundwater</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">30 (15)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. faecalis</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12 (6)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. pallens</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1 (0.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Other <italic>Enterococcus</italic> spp.</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17 (8.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Down-gradient groundwater</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">26 (13)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. faecalis</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21 (10.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. faecium</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1 (0.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. gallinarum</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1 (0.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. raffinosus</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1 (0.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;<italic>E. sulfureus</italic></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1 (0.5)</td></tr><tr><td align="left