"tfn10-ehp0115-001040">a</xref></td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn11-ehp0115-001040">b</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Vancomycin</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.15</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn9-ehp0115-001040"><p><italic>p</italic>-Values were calculated using one-sided Fisher&#x02019;s exact tests.</p></fn><fn id="tfn10-ehp0115-001040"><label>a</label><p>Analyses for clindamycin and virginiamycin resistance were restricted to non&#x02013;<italic>E. faecalis</italic> isolates.</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ehp0115-001040"><label>b</label><p>No <italic>p-</italic>value could be calculated due to zero counts of virginiamycin-resistant isolates in both sample types.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>